<!--
  The transcript window's mute toggle, MUTED (owner ruling 2026-09-22: "the microphone should be
  solid red with the X going through it to show that ... the capture is muted"). Solid red at full
  alpha: the literal is BubbleColours.LIVE_DEFAULT, the one red the panel's furniture uses (the
  resize arrow opposite is the same red), already the contrast guard's binding worst case.

  The X is drawn twice: first a wide near-black border, then the red stroke on top. The border is
  CLIPPED to the mic's own shape, so it only ever cuts the X out of red and never darkens the
  panel: the panel is the user's translucent black, and an unclipped border would draw a dark X
  halo over whatever shows through it. Pinned by MuteTogglePinTest.
-->
